Atlas overlay patch 0011: brand/about-version
Why: the version a person reads in Settings > About, on atlas://version and from the command line
 names Atlas, the WolOS release and the engine, in plain words, and the sentence below the
 copyright points to the credits page instead of naming other projects (reel scene 11, R01). The
 text, the os-release reading and the labels are in the new files chrome/browser/ui/atlas/brand/*
 and chrome/app/atlas/brand_strings.grdp; this patch only calls them. No lower tier: the inherited
 add-helium-versioning patch hard-codes the layout of these strings in the engine files.
Files: chrome/browser/ui/webui/version/version_ui.cc, components/webui/version/resources/about_version.html,
 chrome/app/chrome_main_delegate.cc, chrome/browser/ui/webui/settings/settings_localized_strings_provider.cc
Test filter: *WolosRelease*; journey J-A12 (atlas://version lists Atlas, WolOS, Engine rows; Settings > About line)
Rebase risk: M (the first three files are also patched by add-helium-versioning; the hunks are small and sit next to its lines)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

